+## Experimental visible-output preflight
+
+The opt-in visible-output comparison checks the existing RenderState after output parsing and normal reply/credit handling. A clean pane compares its retained visible cursor and Colors and checks global dirty state. The preflight never cleans global or row dirty flags or constructs a new application Grid. Missing prior drawing and errors require another render; errors remain visible. Pending invalidation is retained. This follows the intent of Herdr App1581a58 shows_change using the safe pinned API, without copying its implementation. The flag is experimental and off by default.
